--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,26 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## SMS verification for sign-up
+
+Copy `.env.example` to `.env` for builds, or set those private environment variables on the Node server. Sign-up fails closed with a helpful message when SMS is not configured; no test codes are accepted.
+
+Create a [Twilio Verify service](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/api/service) with **6-digit codes** and the default **10-minute validity**. Set its service SID, your account SID and auth token in the environment. Enable Verify Fraud Guard, destination country restrictions, and provider/service rate limits for your deployment. The app also enforces a 30-second resend cooldown per session.
+
+Set `TWILIO_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_SID` to an approved [Verify SMS template](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/verification-templates) whose English body is:
+
+```text
+Your DevTools Times verification code is {{code}}.
+
+@your-production-host.example #{{code}}
+```
+
+Replace the host with the actual sign-up page hostname (no scheme, port or path). Every template translation must end with that same origin-bound line, without a trailing signature. Use a separate template for each deployment hostname. This enables WebOTP and compatible OS code suggestions; manual entry works everywhere. Production requires HTTPS.
+
+The same-origin `api/signup` endpoint sends and checks codes through Twilio, binds each challenge to the Astro session and phone number, and calls the existing registration service only after approval. Codes and passwords are never stored in the session. Verified phone numbers are forwarded as `phone`; the external registration service must support persisting that field if durable phone associations are required. This repository cannot change or prevent direct calls to that external service; its own registration policy must enforce phone verification if it remains publicly accessible.
+
+Automated handler tests use mocked provider/registration requests and do not send SMS or start servers: `pnpm dlx tsx --test tests/signup.test.ts`.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
